To initialize the IDF GPIO on an ESP32 board, you can use the following C function:

```c
#include "driver/gpio.h"

void init_gpio(void) {
    gpio_config_t io_conf;
    io_conf.intr_type = GPIO_INTR_DISABLE;
    io_conf.mode = GPIO_MODE_OUTPUT;
    io_conf.pin_bit_mask = (1ULL << GPIO_NUM_2);
    io_conf.pull_down_en = GPIO_PULLDOWN_DISABLE;
    io_conf.pull_up_en = GPIO_PULLUP_DISABLE;
    gpio_config(&io_conf);
}
```

This function configures GPIO2 as an output pin without any pull-up or pull-down resistors. You can modify the `io_conf` structure to suit your specific needs.
